  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "capture-failure-must-not-consume-existing-pcap",
      "severity": "major",
      "disposition": "fixed",
      "reason": "Final active capture uses a new PCAP path and capture && analysis. Independent exact-block shell injections preserve capture exit 42 without analysis, analysis exit 7 after successful capture, and success exit 0. The identical Bash block is bound to the final source; no live capture was run."
    },
    {
      "id": "address-ownership-required-before-elf-decoding",
      "severity": "major",
      "disposition": "fixed",
      "reason": "Final method requires Oops/module/mapping evidence to determine the owning kernel/module/section before choosing matched ELF and trusted relocation. Missing ownership/mapping remains partial, and a resolved line is not identity proof. Host PIE/helper examples support only the stated host scope, not real kernel, module, MCU or board qualification."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Independent AI source-change review; identity is declared, not authenticated. This is not human or GitHub approval, a merge receipt, a release receipt, or authorization to bypass protected checks.",
    "The reviewer did not rerun the complete 102-group suite. It independently reconciled original full log, registered names, timing, completion and all frozen source hashes; separate independent pre-freeze checks retain their actual timestamps and scope.",
    "The 105 cases are Python public-function and bounded-file checks, not 105 CLI or model tasks. The three active-capture cases validate shell control flow only, with no actual TShark/live capture.",
    "The original domain result is 43 checks and 41 process records, including configuration, versions and static checks. Two explanatory source lines changed later; original file hashes and unknown absolute run times remain intact, with exact command-block applicability proved separately.",
    "No real kernel/KASLR/module, MCU, device, HIL, live traffic, mailbox, user runtime installation or native Skill-loading qualification was performed. Host PIE, synthetic PCAP and seeded verified-stage workflow fixtures do not replace those outcomes.",
    "Ruff, mypy and shellcheck executions are not in the supplied local evidence. The final PR HEAD including added receipts still requires all protected remote checks before merge and release.",
    "No real-model A/B, independent holdout, task-success, provider Token, cost or end-to-end latency improvement was measured. Source-byte/profile ratchet changes and test counts are not those benefits.",
    "The 65-identity source audit is not proof that every unchanged Skill was independently executed or all defects eliminated. E1 low-risk implementation routing remains unavailable; this candidate adds no execution authority.",
    "The flaky sampler preserves process outcomes and logs but does not automatically prove framework report completeness or stability; project runners supply their own timeout/cancellation path. Interface scanning remains a limited lexical candidate search.",
    "The retained f538db full run ended after 44 passing groups and one failure with tool-session exit 130; it was not a completed 102-group regression. Historical raw results, source identities and timestamps must not be relabeled as the final run.",
    "Any subsequent source change requires reevaluation of affected evidence and review applicability. Final source Spec/Quality pass does not itself establish subsequent CI, merge, release, installation or product qualification."
  ],
